# Normalize all text files to LF on checkout, matching Prettier's default
# endOfLine="lf". Without this, core.autocrlf=true checks files out with
# CRLF, so `prettier --write .` rewrites nearly every tracked file back to
# LF on every run.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Known binary assets — never subject to text/EOL normalization.
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary

# CLAUDE.md is a symlink to AGENTS.md (git mode 120000). On systems with
# core.symlinks=false it checks out as a plain-text file containing the
# link target; treat it as opaque so git/tooling never rewrites that
# content (e.g. Prettier appending a trailing newline, which corrupts the
# symlink target string).
CLAUDE.md -text -diff
